<h2>Common mistakes to avoid</h2>

<p>There are a few patterns that cost small businesses time and money. Avoid these.</p>

<p><strong>Sending paid traffic to your homepage.</strong> Your homepage is not optimised for conversion. It has navigation links, multiple messages, and no clear single action. Every dollar you spend on ads that land on your homepage is working at half its potential.</p>

<p><strong>Building a funnel when you need a website.</strong> If people cannot find basic information about your business online, a funnel will not help. You need credibility first. Get your website up, then layer funnels on top for specific campaigns.</p>

<p><strong>Building a website when you need a funnel.</strong> If you are launching a new offer and want to test demand quickly, you do not need a full website rebuild. Create a landing page, run some traffic to it, and see if people bite. You can build the rest later.</p>

<p><strong>Treating them as separate systems.</strong> Your website and your funnels should share the same CRM, the same follow-up automations, and the same analytics. When they are disconnected, leads fall through the cracks and you lose visibility into what is working. That fragmentation is exactly what we explore in <a href="/blog/real-cost-of-disconnected-tools">the real cost of disconnected tools</a>.</p>

<p><strong>Over-designing and under-launching.</strong> A simple website that is live today beats a perfect website that launches in six months. The same goes for funnels. Get something out there, measure the results, and improve as you go.</p>

<h2>Start with the question, not the tool</h2>

<p>Before you build anything, ask yourself one question: what do I need this to do? If the answer is "establish credibility and give people a place to learn about my business," build a website. If the answer is "convert this specific audience into leads for this specific offer," build a funnel. If both, build both.</p>

<p>You do not need to choose one forever. Start with whatever addresses your most pressing need right now, and add the other when the time is right.</p>

